    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0485" n="473" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg473"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/179: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Havre</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Havre</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-20T09:00:00+00:00">January 20, 1937—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Forty persons, of whom 20 American citizens recruited in the United States for
                    Spanish Government forces, disembarked from steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lafayette</hi> 18th and about 100 expected to arrive steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Paris</hi> 23rd. Will begin stamping “not valid for
                    travel in Spain” on all passports passengers disembarking not so stamped. Full
                    report by mail follows.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d398-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
